<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part48/9%231> a tmk:Chunk,
        tmk:ManualPassage ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/doc/TMM> ;
    tmk:authorityKind "practice" ;
    tmk:capturedIn tmk:snapshot-c490a9927f1a ;
    tmk:chunkKind "body" ;
    tmk:citesProvision <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s102> ;
    tmk:contentHash "sha256:495c45cf3a30219f540cc11fae1dfe39632905d459184d43095087c8d8e8e864" ;
    tmk:hasCitation <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/cite/TMM/Part48/9%231/prov/0> ;
    tmk:headingPath "Part 48 Removal of a Trade Mark from the Register for Non-use",
        "Part 48.9. Localised use of trade mark" ;
    tmk:onPage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part48/9> ;
    tmk:ordinal 1 ;
    tmk:partId "Part48" ;
    tmk:text "Trade Marks Act 1995 Trade Marks Regulations 1995 Section 102 provides for circumstances where the challenged trade mark is substantially identical or deceptively similar to a registered trade mark owned by the applicant for removal, and: an application to remove the trade mark is made on grounds that it was not used in Australia, or was not used in good faith in Australia, for three year period ending one month before the date of the application, and where the applicant for removal and the opponent have both established use of their respective registered trade marks, and the trade marks are used in different localities, and the applicant’s trade mark is, or will be, subject to geographic limitations or limited to particular export markets. Given these conditions, if non-use has been established in a specified place in Australia or in a specified export market, the court, or the Registrar, may decline to remove the trade mark from the Register. Conditions or limitations, however, may be applied to the registration so that the geographic extents of the registrations become mutually exclusive." ;
    tmk:upstreamRef "TMM/Part48/9#1" .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part49/1/1/1> a tmk:Chunk,
        tmk:ManualPassage ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/doc/TMM> ;
    tmk:authorityKind "practice" ;
    tmk:capturedIn tmk:snapshot-c490a9927f1a ;
    tmk:chunkKind "body" ;
    tmk:citesProvision <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMR1995/r17A.48D> ;
    tmk:contentHash "sha256:5e5c8fdef3f8164d5afa5725c91c4f3547c9e392ec3de770afd2f2a1b24ea8b2" ;
    tmk:hasCitation <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/cite/TMM/Part49/1/1/1/prov/0> ;
    tmk:headingPath "1.1 Form",
        "Part 49 Non-use Procedures",
        "Part 49.1 Application for removal or cessation of protection of a trade mark for non-use" ;
    tmk:onPage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part49/1> ;
    tmk:ordinal 2 ;
    tmk:partId "Part49" ;
    tmk:text "Any person may file an application for removal or cessation of protection of a trade mark for non-use. Please Note: Unless stated otherwise, all references in this Manual part to the removal of a trade mark from the Register also apply to the cessation of protection of a protected international trade mark. See reg 17A.48D. The non-use application should contain the following information: The number of the trade mark which is to be removed The name and address of the person applying for removal That applicant’s address for service in Australia or New Zealand The ground(s) for removal Whether the trade mark is to be removed for some or all of the goods/services Whether the applicant is aware of any court action pending in relation to the trade mark An application form is on the IP Australia website." ;
    tmk:upstreamRef "TMM/Part49/1/1/1" .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part49/1/1/2> a tmk:Chunk,
        tmk:ManualPassage ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/doc/TMM> ;
    tmk:authorityKind "practice" ;
    tmk:capturedIn tmk:snapshot-c490a9927f1a ;
    tmk:chunkKind "body" ;
    tmk:citesPassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part4/x-relevant-legislation15> ;
    tmk:contentHash "sha256:8344850a49be87dc59665d5fd11d22c09747c047c1f20f98fc83cbdebd9ad0ed" ;
    tmk:hasCitation <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/cite/TMM/Part49/1/1/2/internal/0> ;
    tmk:headingPath "1.2 Fee",
        "Part 49 Non-use Procedures",
        "Part 49.1 Application for removal or cessation of protection of a trade mark for non-use" ;
    tmk:onPage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part49/1> ;
    tmk:ordinal 3 ;
    tmk:partId "Part49" ;
    tmk:text "The applicant must pay the fee for filing the non-use application (see Item 13 in Schedule 9 to the Trade Marks Regulations 1995.) The application will not be processed until the fee is paid. Part 4 Fees" ;
    tmk:upstreamRef "TMM/Part49/1/1/2" .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part49/1/1/6> a tmk:Chunk,
        tmk:ManualPassage ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/doc/TMM> ;
    tmk:authorityKind "practice" ;
    tmk:capturedIn tmk:snapshot-c490a9927f1a ;
    tmk:chunkKind "body" ;
    tmk:citesProvision <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMR1995/r21.4> ;
    tmk:contentHash "sha256:7bdf0d19ac3ca0f1626b9d162a9c4e8b46a262939fe790704f280e0792b6924b" ;
    tmk:hasCitation <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/cite/TMM/Part49/1/1/6/prov/0> ;
    tmk:headingPath "1.6 Processing",
        "Part 49 Non-use Procedures",
        "Part 49.1 Application for removal or cessation of protection of a trade mark for non-use" ;
    tmk:onPage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part49/1> ;
    tmk:ordinal 7 ;
    tmk:partId "Part49" ;
    tmk:text "The Registrar will check whether the non-use application is in the proper form. If it is not, the applicant will be advised. If it is possible to bring it into the proper form the applicant will be given an opportunity to do so. If it is not possible, the application will be deemed not filed (reg 21.4) and returned to the applicant. The filing fee will be refunded." ;
    tmk:upstreamRef "TMM/Part49/1/1/6" .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part49/1/1/9> a tmk:Chunk,
        tmk:ManualPassage ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/doc/TMM> ;
    tmk:authorityKind "practice" ;
    tmk:capturedIn tmk:snapshot-c490a9927f1a ;
    tmk:chunkKind "body" ;
    tmk:citesProvision <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s97> ;
    tmk:contentHash "sha256:f2133188ba8071b7f49bb4c81fa4ad877409379e8442a9c530938ddd57a94275" ;
    tmk:hasCitation <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/cite/TMM/Part49/1/1/9/prov/0> ;
    tmk:headingPath "1.9 Trade mark removed",
        "Part 49 Non-use Procedures",
        "Part 49.1 Application for removal or cessation of protection of a trade mark for non-use" ;
    tmk:onPage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part49/1> ;
    tmk:ordinal 10 ;
    tmk:partId "Part49" ;
    tmk:text "If nobody opposes removal in the time allowed to do so and the Registrar is satisfied the non-use application is in order the trade mark will be removed to the extent specified in the application (s 97)." ;
    tmk:upstreamRef "TMM/Part49/1/1/9" .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part49/2/1-acts-interpretation-act-1901-cth-s-25c> a tmk:Chunk,
        tmk:ManualPassage ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/doc/TMM> ;
