    tmk:lastAmended "2026-02-11" ;
    tmk:partId "Part35" ;
    tmk:sourceUrl "https://manuals.ipaustralia.gov.au/trademark/1.-what-is-a-certification-trade-mark-"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    tmk:upstreamRef "TMM/Part35/1" .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part35/11%231> a tmk:Chunk,
        tmk:ManualPassage ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/doc/TMM> ;
    tmk:authorityKind "practice" ;
    tmk:capturedIn tmk:snapshot-c490a9927f1a ;
    tmk:chunkKind "body" ;
    tmk:citesPassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part43/7> ;
    tmk:citesProvision <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s180>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s180A>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMR1995/r10.1> ;
    tmk:contentHash "sha256:9b6b028006338696b5dd18cdb12a0685c066059a5ac74b26e7ea4d79c7c8e108" ;
    tmk:hasCitation <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/cite/TMM/Part35/11%231/internal/0>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/cite/TMM/Part35/11%231/prov/0>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/cite/TMM/Part35/11%231/prov/1>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/cite/TMM/Part35/11%231/prov/2> ;
    tmk:headingPath "35.11. Transmission of certification trade marks",
        "Part 35 Certification Trade Marks" ;
    tmk:onPage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part35/11> ;
    tmk:ordinal 1 ;
    tmk:partId "Part35" ;
    tmk:text "Trade Marks Act 1995 Trade Marks Regulations 1995 There are no provisions under the Trade Marks Act 1995 requiring consent from the Commission before the transmission of a certification trade mark, whether registered or the subject of an application for registration. Transmission of a certification trade mark is most likely to occur by operation of law and there is then no basis for obtaining consent. Sections 180 and 180A deal only with assignment, as does regulation 10.1 (as amended by Trade Marks Amendment Regulations 2001 (No. 3)). The process of recording transmission of a certification trade mark is covered in Part 43 of the Manual. Part 43 Assignment and Transmission - 7. Transmission of certification trade marks" ;
    tmk:upstreamRef "TMM/Part35/11#1" .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part35/4/4/1> a tmk:Chunk,
        tmk:ManualPassage ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/doc/TMM> ;
    tmk:authorityKind "practice" ;
    tmk:capturedIn tmk:snapshot-c490a9927f1a ;
    tmk:chunkKind "body" ;
    tmk:citesProvision <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s177>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s177(2)>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s177(2)(a)>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s177(2)(b)> ;
    tmk:contentHash "sha256:794c72437e21186d3df0ecb6b0a1b07a06f6eeb5a59d41ca4e674d263c263938" ;
    tmk:hasCitation <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/cite/TMM/Part35/4/4/1/prov/0>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/cite/TMM/Part35/4/4/1/prov/1>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/cite/TMM/Part35/4/4/1/prov/2>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/cite/TMM/Part35/4/4/1/prov/3> ;
    tmk:headingPath "35.4. The registrability of certification trade marks",
        "4.1 Certification trade mark not distinguishing certified goods or services",
        "Part 35 Certification Trade Marks" ;
    tmk:onPage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part35/4> ;
    tmk:ordinal 2 ;
    tmk:partId "Part35" ;
    tmk:text "Section 177(2) sets out the criteria to be applied in deciding whether or not a certification trade mark is capable of distinguishing the goods or services certified by the applicant, or an approved certifier, from goods or services which are not so certified. In deciding this question, the following must be taken into account: the extent to which the certification trade mark is inherently adapted to distinguish the certified goods and or services in Australia (section 177(2)(a)); or the extent to which the certification trade mark has become adapted to distinguish the certified goods and or services because of use or any other circumstances (section 177(2)(b)). If the certification trade mark is not prima facie capable of distinguishing the certified goods and or services, substantial evidence of use may be required to satisfy the Registrar that the certification trade mark has become adapted to distinguish. Importantly, intended use is not a relevant consideration for the purposes of section 177. Other circumstances for the purposes of section 177(2)(b) might include, for example, the proposals for implementation of the certification scheme and the extent to which it has been advertised and made known in the relevant market. If a certification trade mark is accepted on the basis of evidence of use or other circumstances, the following endorsement is entered on the Register: Provisions of paragraph 177(2)(b) applied." ;
    tmk:upstreamRef "TMM/Part35/4/4/1" .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part38/2> a tmk:Page ;
    rdfs:label "2. Reasons for revocation"@en-AU ;
