<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s112> a tmk:LegislativeProvision ;
    rdfs:label "Object of Part"@en-AU ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/doc/TMA1995> ;
    tmk:authorityKind "law" ;
    tmk:authorityStatus tmk:Current ;
    tmk:capturedIn tmk:snapshot-c490a9927f1a ;
    tmk:contentHash "sha256:da28bff083bfd62a9cb5dbbada51449dd5eadbb757b664545350254d1fcad8ba" ;
    tmk:text "This Part makes provision: (a) for recording in the Register claims to interests in, and rights in respect of, registered trade marks that may not be so recorded under another Part; and (b) for the Registrar to keep a record of claims to interests in, and rights in respect of, trade marks for which registration is sought. Note: For registered trade mark see section 6." ;
    tmk:upstreamRef "TMA1995/s112" .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s120(1)> a tmk:LegislativeUnit ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/doc/TMA1995>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s120> ;
    tmk:authorityKind "law" ;
    tmk:authorityStatus tmk:Current ;
    tmk:capturedIn tmk:snapshot-c490a9927f1a ;
    tmk:contentHash "sha256:5330fa04caf56f950025e213a65516a72c046d0306afb263059971822f9bbf28" ;
    tmk:ordinal 1 ;
    tmk:text "(1) A person infringes a registered trade mark if the person uses as a trade mark a sign that is substantially identical with, or deceptively similar to, the trade mark in relation to goods or services in respect of which the trade mark is registered." ;
    tmk:upstreamRef "TMA1995/s120(1)" .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s15(1)> tmk:authorityStatus tmk:NotHeld ;
    tmk:upstreamRef "TMA1995/s15(1)" .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s15(1)(a)> tmk:authorityStatus tmk:NotHeld ;
    tmk:upstreamRef "TMA1995/s15(1)(a)" .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s15(1)(e)> tmk:authorityStatus tmk:NotHeld ;
    tmk:upstreamRef "TMA1995/s15(1)(e)" .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s16E> tmk:authorityStatus tmk:NotHeld ;
    tmk:upstreamRef "TMA1995/s16E" .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s185(1)> a tmk:LegislativeUnit ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/doc/TMA1995>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s185> ;
    tmk:authorityKind "law" ;
    tmk:authorityStatus tmk:Current ;
    tmk:capturedIn tmk:snapshot-c490a9927f1a ;
    tmk:contentHash "sha256:f375000bf09412d3f2c7765806ec0fb5c1fab4f628bae9eedbae68ccbb1d808a" ;
    tmk:ordinal 1 ;
    tmk:text "(1) If, because of the extent to which a registered trade mark has been used in relation to all or any of the goods or services in respect of which it is registered, it is likely that its use in relation to other goods or services will be taken to indicate that there is a connection between those other goods or services and the registered owner of the trade mark, the trade mark may, on the application of the registered owner, be registered as a defensive trade mark in respect of any or all of those other goods or services." ;
    tmk:upstreamRef "TMA1995/s185(1)" .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s224(7)> a tmk:LegislativeUnit ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/doc/TMA1995>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s224> ;
    tmk:authorityKind "law" ;
    tmk:authorityStatus tmk:Current ;
    tmk:capturedIn tmk:snapshot-c490a9927f1a ;
    tmk:contentHash "sha256:4cccf2e6408d54b1fed376981f36e05c39b7145b87e4a9a8c1631fafd723a7b3" ;
    tmk:ordinal 18 ;
    tmk:text "(7) An application may be made to the Administrative Review Tribunal for the review of a decision of the Registrar not to extend the time for the doing of a relevant act." ;
    tmk:upstreamRef "TMA1995/s224(7)" .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s23(4)> tmk:authorityStatus tmk:NotHeld ;
    tmk:upstreamRef "TMA1995/s23(4)" .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s3> a tmk:LegislativeProvision ;
    rdfs:label "Act binds the Crown"@en-AU ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/doc/TMA1995> ;
    tmk:authorityKind "law" ;
    tmk:authorityStatus tmk:Current ;
    tmk:capturedIn tmk:snapshot-c490a9927f1a ;
    tmk:contentHash "sha256:b59d192ac1003234082fff6706df6c8f073df55600fa16e16905888f89953427" ;
    tmk:text "(1) This Act binds the Crown in right of the Commonwealth, of each of the States, of the Australian Capital Territory and of the Northern Territory. (2) Nothing in this Act makes the Crown liable to be prosecuted for an offence." ;
    tmk:upstreamRef "TMA1995/s3" .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s33(1)> a tmk:LegislativeUnit ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/doc/TMA1995>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s33> ;
    tmk:authorityKind "law" ;
    tmk:authorityStatus tmk:Current ;
    tmk:capturedIn tmk:snapshot-c490a9927f1a ;
    tmk:contentHash "sha256:a071ed6dcfc5c0c8ef6f02ab77cb17839891e28ff5d1e8a8941caf2ce8eed167" ;
    tmk:ordinal 1 ;
    tmk:text "(1) The Registrar must, after the examination, accept the application unless he or she is satisfied that:" ;
    tmk:upstreamRef "TMA1995/s33(1)" .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s33(3)> a tmk:LegislativeUnit ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/doc/TMA1995>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s33> ;
    tmk:authorityKind "law" ;
    tmk:authorityStatus tmk:Current ;
    tmk:capturedIn tmk:snapshot-c490a9927f1a ;
    tmk:contentHash "sha256:da8ed57768f6a081a25834ad5b025207a615144d9de6e31df439f6d67e987f40" ;
    tmk:ordinal 7 ;
    tmk:text "(3) If the Registrar is satisfied that:" ;
    tmk:upstreamRef "TMA1995/s33(3)" .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s33(4)> a tmk:LegislativeUnit ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/doc/TMA1995>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s33> ;
    tmk:authorityKind "law" ;
    tmk:authorityStatus tmk:Current ;
    tmk:capturedIn tmk:snapshot-c490a9927f1a ;
    tmk:contentHash "sha256:bf8c0b25fc506600b605bbda09111bada1f72bcb3bbe7eb03bcb5b890decb812" ;
    tmk:ordinal 12 ;
    tmk:text "(4) The Registrar may not reject an application without giving the applicant an opportunity of being heard." ;
    tmk:upstreamRef "TMA1995/s33(4)" .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s35> a tmk:LegislativeProvision ;
    rdfs:label "Appeal"@en-AU ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/doc/TMA1995> ;
    tmk:authorityKind "law" ;
    tmk:authorityStatus tmk:Current ;
    tmk:capturedIn tmk:snapshot-c490a9927f1a ;
    tmk:contentHash "sha256:ecf843a502d95cd02974fec8a61c0e86740818500621aa5710a5c9c4ffb34fd0" ;
    tmk:text "The applicant may appeal to the Federal Court or the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 2) against a decision of the Registrar: (a) to accept the application subject to conditions or limitations; or (b) to reject the application. Note: For applicant see section 6." ;
    tmk:upstreamRef "TMA1995/s35" .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s46(2)> a tmk:LegislativeUnit ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/doc/TMA1995>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s46> ;
    tmk:authorityKind "law" ;
    tmk:authorityStatus tmk:Current ;
    tmk:capturedIn tmk:snapshot-c490a9927f1a ;
    tmk:contentHash "sha256:26f9acbc7a775565bbb0687dcbaad5212f5436c7d56ef270c5c256da7392347a" ;
    tmk:ordinal 6 ;
    tmk:text "(2) When a divisional application is made, the Registrar must, unless the parent application has lapsed, amend the parent application by excluding the goods and/or services in respect of which the divisional application is made." ;
    tmk:upstreamRef "TMA1995/s46(2)" .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s51(1)> a tmk:LegislativeUnit ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/doc/TMA1995>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s51> ;
    tmk:authorityKind "law" ;
    tmk:authorityStatus tmk:Current ;
    tmk:capturedIn tmk:snapshot-c490a9927f1a ;
    tmk:contentHash "sha256:9ac2fb40c863256d91bdd616a40612edf17eadf7fb95ea1b36e347320a5807a1" ;
    tmk:ordinal 1 ;
    tmk:text "(1) A person may make a single application under subsection 27(1) for the registration of 2 or more trade marks in respect of goods and/or services if the trade marks resemble each other in material particulars and differ only in respect of one or more of the following matters:" ;
    tmk:upstreamRef "TMA1995/s51(1)" .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s51(1)(a)> a tmk:LegislativeUnit ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/doc/TMA1995>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s51> ;
    tmk:authorityKind "law" ;
    tmk:authorityStatus tmk:Current ;
    tmk:capturedIn tmk:snapshot-c490a9927f1a ;
    tmk:contentHash "sha256:6c1cfdcc51bed4645265fc340177c51b34a4b7839fe79b8d1151ea5895117b2c" ;
    tmk:ordinal 2 ;
    tmk:text "(a) statements or representations as to the goods or services in relation to which the trade marks are used or are intended to be used;" ;
    tmk:upstreamRef "TMA1995/s51(1)(a)" .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s65(4)> a tmk:LegislativeUnit ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/doc/TMA1995>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s65> ;
    tmk:authorityKind "law" ;
    tmk:authorityStatus tmk:Current ;
    tmk:capturedIn tmk:snapshot-c490a9927f1a ;
    tmk:contentHash "sha256:edce598a37fb83c439ee6ef339338a5608773628e00b9a7b788a0ae32cd18dda" ;
    tmk:ordinal 4 ;
    tmk:text "(4) An amendment may be made to correct an error in the classification of goods or services specified in the application." ;
    tmk:upstreamRef "TMA1995/s65(4)" .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s65(5)> a tmk:LegislativeUnit ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/doc/TMA1995>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s65> ;
    tmk:authorityKind "law" ;
    tmk:authorityStatus tmk:Current ;
    tmk:capturedIn tmk:snapshot-c490a9927f1a ;
    tmk:contentHash "sha256:ec058fa304ba8cb0915a561226d15e6c1d6027e0e5876fd7bad58f33e1d44e73" ;
    tmk:ordinal 5 ;
    tmk:text "(5) An amendment may be made to add to the class or classes of goods or services specified in the application one or more other classes of goods or services if the Registrar is of the opinion that it is fair and reasonable in all the circumstances to do so." ;
    tmk:upstreamRef "TMA1995/s65(5)" .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s71> a tmk:LegislativeProvision ;
    rdfs:label "Notification of registration"@en-AU ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/doc/TMA1995> ;
    tmk:authorityKind "law" ;
    tmk:authorityStatus tmk:Current ;
    tmk:capturedIn tmk:snapshot-c490a9927f1a ;
    tmk:contentHash "sha256:c680bc2f9ad43c996b519157722d556115b27828715615b7c91c425da75d140f" ;
    tmk:text "When a trade mark has been registered, the Registrar must: (a) publish the registration in accordance with the regulations; and (b) give to the registered owner of the trade mark a certificate of registration in an approved form. Note: For registered owner and approved form see section 6." ;
    tmk:upstreamRef "TMA1995/s71" .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s74(1)> a tmk:LegislativeUnit ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/doc/TMA1995> ;
    tmk:authorityKind "law" ;
    tmk:authorityStatus tmk:Current ;
    tmk:capturedIn tmk:snapshot-c490a9927f1a ;
    tmk:contentHash "sha256:a8694c14550c965880b1b3a8f15c9bd05b1c98f80578d70fe7439e3ac31b5ceb" ;
    tmk:text "(1) An applicant for the registration of a trade mark, or the registered owner of a registered trade mark, may, by notice in writing given to the Registrar, disclaim any exclusive right to use, or authorise the use of, a specified part of the trade mark." ;
    tmk:upstreamRef "TMA1995/s74(1)" .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s80> a tmk:LegislativeProvision ;
    rdfs:label "Status of unrenewed trade mark"@en-AU ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/doc/TMA1995> ;
    tmk:authorityKind "law" ;
    tmk:authorityStatus tmk:Current ;
    tmk:capturedIn tmk:snapshot-c490a9927f1a ;
    tmk:contentHash "sha256:6d42364239b82722992deeaac0a27a89299280c80c259ed870bf3066665f347a" ;
    tmk:text "If: (a) the registration of a trade mark (unrenewed trade mark) has not been renewed under section 77 or 79; and (b) an application for the registration of a trade mark is made, or has already been made, by a person other than the person who was registered as the owner of the unrenewed trade mark; the unrenewed trade mark is taken to be a registered trade mark for the purposes of the application at any time when the registration of the unrenewed trade mark could have been renewed under section 79." ;
    tmk:upstreamRef "TMA1995/s80" .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s85> a tmk:LegislativeProvision ;
    rdfs:label "Amendment to correct error or omission"@en-AU ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/doc/TMA1995> ;
    tmk:authorityKind "law" ;
    tmk:authorityStatus tmk:Current ;
    tmk:capturedIn tmk:snapshot-c490a9927f1a ;
    tmk:contentHash "sha256:a0408ab4ba378332bf7d225f73cced18c81cd48b711cb4ff02888ff0c729d65b" ;
    tmk:text "A prescribed court may, on the application of an aggrieved person, order that the Register be rectified by: (a) entering in the Register particulars that were wrongly omitted from it; or (b) correcting any error in an entry in the Register. Note: For prescribed court see section 190." ;
    tmk:upstreamRef "TMA1995/s85" .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s9(2)> a tmk:LegislativeUnit ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/doc/TMA1995>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s9> ;
    tmk:authorityKind "law" ;
    tmk:authorityStatus tmk:Current ;
    tmk:capturedIn tmk:snapshot-c490a9927f1a ;
    tmk:contentHash "sha256:13ed27a7fec9d3e9f37cabb7a0c50b79878b1797831257e4fef1c1bdbbde2f65" ;
    tmk:ordinal 10 ;
    tmk:text "(2) In subparagraph (1)(b)(i):" ;
    tmk:upstreamRef "TMA1995/s9(2)" .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s92(4)(a)> a tmk:LegislativeUnit ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/doc/TMA1995>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s92> ;
    tmk:authorityKind "law" ;
    tmk:authorityStatus tmk:Current ;
    tmk:capturedIn tmk:snapshot-c490a9927f1a ;
    tmk:contentHash "sha256:e1c8c0b6719934236d8533bfb45be28fc3c71ad35000123563767462d6a76cd1" ;
    tmk:ordinal 8 ;
    tmk:text "(a) that, on the day on which the application for the registration of the trade mark was filed, the applicant for registration had no intention in good faith:" ;
    tmk:upstreamRef "TMA1995/s92(4)(a)" .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s93> a tmk:LegislativeProvision ;
    rdfs:label "Time for making application"@en-AU ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/doc/TMA1995> ;
    tmk:authorityKind "law" ;
    tmk:authorityStatus tmk:Current ;
    tmk:capturedIn tmk:snapshot-c490a9927f1a ;
    tmk:contentHash "sha256:54ef06c1062e631e12fa53034f8b4e92c210b28961e110e29dec7f41c8b04768" ;
    tmk:text "(1) A nonuse application on the ground mentioned in paragraph 92(4)(a) may be made at any time after the filing date in respect of the application for the registration of the trade mark. Note: For filing date see section 6. (2) A nonuse application on the ground mentioned in paragraph 92(4)(b) may only be made after a period of 3 years beginning from the date the particulars of the trade mark were entered into the Register under section 69. Note: The registration of a trade mark is taken to have effect earlier than the date the particulars of the trade mark are entered into the Register (see sections 72 and 239A)." ;
    tmk:upstreamRef "TMA1995/s93" .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s94> a tmk:LegislativeProvision ;
    rdfs:label "Referral to court"@en-AU ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/doc/TMA1995> ;
    tmk:authorityKind "law" ;
    tmk:authorityStatus tmk:Current ;
    tmk:capturedIn tmk:snapshot-c490a9927f1a ;
    tmk:contentHash "sha256:0d1b6f3afaafdf17824f4927f9301a256f0b62cb6bdf515fedfd645914f06834" ;
    tmk:text "If: (a) an application has been made to the Registrar under subsection 92(1); and (b) the Registrar is of the opinion that the matter should be decided by a prescribed court; the Registrar may refer the matter to such a court and the court may hear and determine the matter as if an application had been made to it under subsection 92(3)." ;
    tmk:upstreamRef "TMA1995/s94" .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part10/1%231> a tmk:Chunk,
        tmk:ManualPassage ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/doc/TMM> ;
    tmk:authorityKind "practice" ;
    tmk:capturedIn tmk:snapshot-c490a9927f1a ;
    tmk:chunkKind "body" ;
    tmk:citesProvision <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s27>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s27(2)(c)>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s28>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s28(a)>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s28(b)>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s6> ;
    tmk:contentHash "sha256:f730f4012ba3ba34c936f055982bda25e1df68a6daf876594f86438834e74cb0" ;
    tmk:hasCitation <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/cite/TMM/Part10/1%231/prov/0>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/cite/TMM/Part10/1%231/prov/1>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/cite/TMM/Part10/1%231/prov/2>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/cite/TMM/Part10/1%231/prov/3>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/cite/TMM/Part10/1%231/prov/4>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/cite/TMM/Part10/1%231/prov/5> ;
    tmk:headingPath "10.1. Formality requirements - Name",
        "Part 10 Details of Formality Requirements" ;
    tmk:onPage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part10/1> ;
    tmk:ordinal 1 ;
    tmk:partId "Part10" ;
    tmk:text "Federal Register of Legislation - Trade Marks Regulations 1995 Federal Register of Legislation - Trade Marks Act 1995 Under section 6 of the Act “person includes a body of persons, whether incorporated or not.” However, subsection 27(2)(c) states that the application must be made by a person or persons having legal personality. Therefore an applicant for registration of a trade mark under section 27 may be an individual, a company, an incorporated club or association, an incorporated entity or any combination of these who together own a trade mark. Applications lodged in the name of trusts, business names, trading styles, unincorporated associations, clubs, partnerships or societies cannot be accepted since these entities do not have a legal personality. Applications for collective trade marks however will continue to be capable of being owned by an unincorporated association. The circumstances under which two or more persons may apply for registration of a trade mark are set out in section 28 of the Act. Paragraph 28(a) of the Act covers the circumstances where the trade mark is used at all times on behalf of all the applicants. Paragraph 28(b) provides for a joint trade connection between two or more applicants and the goods and/or services in relation to, or upon which, the trade mark is to be used. This encompasses joint ventures between companies or individuals who may not be trading together but who each has a role in putting the goods and/or services which carry the trade mark into the marketplace." ;
    tmk:upstreamRef "TMM/Part10/1#1" .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part13/2%231~1> a tmk:Chunk,
        tmk:ManualPassage ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/doc/TMM> ;
    tmk:authorityKind "practice" ;
    tmk:capturedIn tmk:snapshot-c490a9927f1a ;
    tmk:chunkKind "body" ;
    tmk:citesCase <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/CASE/2011/ATMO/63>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/CASE/2025/ATMO/227> ;
    tmk:citesProvision <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s51>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s51(1)>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s51(1)(a)>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s51(1)(a)(b)> ;
    tmk:contentHash "sha256:da73568cd8d272b341798cf47ac4902f3ea75c9588bd3affcd88dde92d47adc8" ;
    tmk:hasCitation <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/cite/TMM/Part13/2%231~1/case/0>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/cite/TMM/Part13/2%231~1/case/1>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/cite/TMM/Part13/2%231~1/prov/0>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/cite/TMM/Part13/2%231~1/prov/1>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/cite/TMM/Part13/2%231~1/prov/2>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/cite/TMM/Part13/2%231~1/prov/3> ;
    tmk:headingPath "13.2. Material Particulars",
        "Part 13 Application to Register a Series of Trade Marks" ;
    tmk:onPage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part13/2> ;
    tmk:ordinal 1 ;
    tmk:partId "Part13" ;
    tmk:text "Trade Marks Act 1995 Trade Mark Regulations 1995 Series applications are intended to be allowed “only for minor and obvious variations” of a trade mark (Explanatory Memorandum, Trade Marks Amendment Bill 2006, 5.5). Section 51(1) presents two requirements for a valid series (that is, a series of trade marks that can be included together in a single application): the trade marks must resemble each other in material particulars; and the trade marks must differ only in the ways allowed in paragraphs 51(1)(a), (b) and (c). In Ecospecifier Pty Ltd [2011] ATMO 63 at [12], the Delegate noted that a “material particular” in respect of a trade mark (for the purpose of section 51) must be “a feature which is important, essential and non-trivial and which is also that portion of the trade mark likely to be recalled as being a trade mark”. In Tawfek Mahmoud [2025] ATMO 227, the Delegate said (at [23]): The Applicant’s submissions appear to be based on the premise that as long as each of the marks share some (emphasis added) material particulars the series as a whole shall be valid. This is not correct. Rather each of the Trade Marks must share all material particulars for the mark to be a valid series mark. The fact that each of the Trade Marks contains a derivation of the word ‘link’ is not sufficient for me to find that they resemble each other in material particulars; rather the entirety of each mark’s material particulars must resemble each other’s material particulars, save for the differences outlined in subsections 51(1)(a)(b) and (c). To take an obvious example the mark WORLD LINKS does not resemble THE AUSTRALIAN LINKEDIN. Indeed, the only similarity between the two marks is that they share the 4 letters ‘link’ in part of those marks. They are otherwise utterly dissimilar. The effect of section 51 of as a whole is that the material particulars in each trade mark of the series must essentially be the same. In many cases, the material particulars will be entirely comprised of the distinctive elements of the trade mark. However, in some cases, descriptive or non-distinctive elements can form part of the material particulars of a trade mark – particularly if their size and presentation within the trade mark make them identifying features, or if the trade marks are entirely comprised of descriptive material." ;
    tmk:upstreamRef "TMM/Part13/2#1~1" .

