<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMR1995/r17A.11> a tmk:LegislativeProvision ;
    rdfs:label "Purpose of Division"@en-AU ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/doc/TMR1995> ;
    tmk:authorityKind "law" ;
    tmk:authorityStatus tmk:Current ;
    tmk:capturedIn tmk:snapshot-c490a9927f1a ;
    tmk:contentHash "sha256:1d9918565d88fec90220b50629726a98ef2e8340fa0bfd20fe198ab5d3f40076" ;
    tmk:text "This Division makes provision for dealing with a request to extend to Australia the protection resulting from international registration of a trade mark." ;
    tmk:upstreamRef "TMR1995/r17A.11" .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMR1995/r17A.34D> a tmk:LegislativeProvision ;
    rdfs:label "Extension of time for filing—grant"@en-AU ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/doc/TMR1995> ;
    tmk:authorityKind "law" ;
    tmk:authorityStatus tmk:Current ;
    tmk:capturedIn tmk:snapshot-c490a9927f1a ;
    tmk:contentHash "sha256:6f2c2bebde3d0ce4d61ca39f89426c3f8db39a539d2a6c9a36d48da152aa17ff" ;
    tmk:text "(1) The Registrar may grant a request under subregulation 17A.34C(1) for an extension of time if the Registrar is satisfied that the grounds set out in the request justify the extension. (2) However, if the request is made after the period for filing the notice or statement of grounds and particulars has ended, the Registrar must not grant the extension unless the Registrar is satisfied that there is sufficient reason for the delay in making the request. (3) The Registrar must decide the length of the extended period having regard to what is reasonable in the circumstances." ;
    tmk:upstreamRef "TMR1995/r17A.34D" .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMR1995/r17A.37> a tmk:LegislativeProvision ;
    rdfs:label "Notice that trade mark is a protected international trade mark"@en-AU ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/doc/TMR1995> ;
    tmk:authorityKind "law" ;
    tmk:authorityStatus tmk:Current ;
    tmk:capturedIn tmk:snapshot-c490a9927f1a ;
    tmk:contentHash "sha256:fd7ca4282db0608668f18b97e7d1e27ad315fa972c1e0946a5e2f83a0470a087" ;
    tmk:text "(1) If a trade mark becomes a protected international trade mark, the Registrar must: (a) publish that fact in a computer database maintained by the Trade Marks Office; and (b) record that fact in the Record of International Registrations. (2) The notice and record must include particulars of the conditions (if any) and the limitations (if any) to which the protection is subject. (3) As soon as practicable after receiving notice that a trade mark is a protected international trade mark, the holder must notify the Registrar, in writing, of the holder’s address for service in Australia or New Zealand." ;
    tmk:upstreamRef "TMR1995/r17A.37" .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMR1995/r17A.42> a tmk:LegislativeProvision ;
    rdfs:label "Failure to renew international registration"@en-AU ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/doc/TMR1995> ;
    tmk:authorityKind "law" ;
    tmk:authorityStatus tmk:Current ;
    tmk:capturedIn tmk:snapshot-c490a9927f1a ;
    tmk:contentHash "sha256:b074b42c7a464aac7e5dfe51217e4cfd1e8a25f3418f96b836e783b5abada41e" ;
    tmk:text "(1) If the international registration of a trade mark that is a protected international trade mark is not renewed, the trade mark ceases to be a protected international trade mark when the international registration expires. (2) However, if: (a) the international registration of a trade mark that is a protected international trade mark (unrenewed protected international trade mark) is not renewed; and (b) an application for the registration of the trade mark, or an IRDA, is made, or has already been made, by a person other than the holder of the unrenewed protected international trade mark; the unrenewed protected international trade mark is taken to be a protected international trade mark for the purposes of the application or the IRDA, at any time when the registration of the unrenewed protected international trade mark could have been renewed under Article 7 of the Protocol." ;
    tmk:upstreamRef "TMR1995/r17A.42" .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMR1995/r17A.48F> a tmk:LegislativeProvision ;
    rdfs:label "Filing of notice of opposition"@en-AU ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/doc/TMR1995> ;
    tmk:authorityKind "law" ;
    tmk:authorityStatus tmk:Current ;
    tmk:capturedIn tmk:snapshot-c490a9927f1a ;
    tmk:contentHash "sha256:a2b8eade1352d74feb3b6d5732ec4808e4929486d34125328aaca13ced2e8e66" ;
    tmk:text "A notice of opposition is taken to be filed when the notice of intention to oppose and the statement of grounds and particulars have been filed under regulations 17A.48G and 17A.48J." ;
    tmk:upstreamRef "TMR1995/r17A.48F" .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMR1995/r17A.51> a tmk:LegislativeProvision ;
    rdfs:label "Application of Division"@en-AU ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/doc/TMR1995> ;
    tmk:authorityKind "law" ;
    tmk:authorityStatus tmk:Current ;
    tmk:capturedIn tmk:snapshot-c490a9927f1a ;
    tmk:contentHash "sha256:3dff0af008604a9da848209df746efd2e047de21cccd81bfac909d886ade440a" ;
    tmk:text "This Division applies if: (a) the international registration of a trade mark is cancelled, in whole or in part, by the International Bureau at the request of the Office of origin, in accordance with Article 6(4) of the Protocol; and (b) the trade mark is the subject of an IRDA or is a protected international trade mark; and (c) within 3 months after the date on which the international registration was cancelled, the person who held the international registration files with the Trade Marks Office an application for registration of the trade mark (a transformation application); and (d) the transformation application is in relation to any of the goods and services to which the cancellation applies that were listed in the IRDA, or covered by the protected international trade mark, immediately before the cancellation." ;
    tmk:upstreamRef "TMR1995/r17A.51" .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMR1995/r17A.9> a tmk:LegislativeProvision ;
    rdfs:label "Time limit for Registrar to send application to International Bureau"@en-AU ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/doc/TMR1995> ;
    tmk:authorityKind "law" ;
    tmk:authorityStatus tmk:Current ;
    tmk:capturedIn tmk:snapshot-c490a9927f1a ;
    tmk:contentHash "sha256:1e636034d4cec06dc021dd79f3e75286bc2a85448ba0af97ba8530806c82316d" ;
    tmk:text "The Registrar must take all reasonable steps to ensure that the application is received by the International Bureau within 2 months after the date on which it is filed." ;
    tmk:upstreamRef "TMR1995/r17A.9" .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMR1995/r19.1> a tmk:LegislativeProvision ;
    rdfs:label "Trade Marks Office and suboffices—business hours"@en-AU ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/doc/TMR1995> ;
    tmk:authorityKind "law" ;
    tmk:authorityStatus tmk:Current ;
    tmk:capturedIn tmk:snapshot-c490a9927f1a ;
    tmk:contentHash "sha256:8f7b1d00259b7ef4f35a8e7790f65b666adadbaadb6800a3c9dd6478e245a65b" ;
    tmk:text "The hours of business of the Trade Marks Office and each suboffice (if any) of the Trade Marks Office are from 9 am to 5 pm on each day other than: (a) a Saturday or a Sunday; or (b) a public holiday: (i) where the Office or suboffice (if any) is located; or (ii) for the purposes of the Australian Public Service in that place." ;
    tmk:upstreamRef "TMR1995/r19.1" .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMR1995/r8.4> a tmk:LegislativeProvision ;
    rdfs:label "Amendment because of inconsistency with international agreements—notice of opposition"@en-AU ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/doc/TMR1995> ;
    tmk:authorityKind "law" ;
    tmk:authorityStatus tmk:Current ;
    tmk:capturedIn tmk:snapshot-c490a9927f1a ;
    tmk:contentHash "sha256:ac1b56f3f7b1510fcca62369e5dfc8d92271d572bdc202b9ec84e812a137d484" ;
    tmk:text "(1) For subsection 83A(4) of the Act, a person may oppose a request for amendment by filing a notice of opposition with the Registrar. (2) A notice of opposition must be: (a) in an approved form; and (b) filed within 1 month after the request for amendment is published in a computer database maintained by the Trade Marks Office in accordance with regulation 8.3A. (3) The Registrar must give a copy of the notice to the registered owner of the registered trade mark." ;
    tmk:upstreamRef "TMR1995/r8.4" .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMR1995/sch9> a tmk:LegislativeProvision ;
    rdfs:label "Fees"@en-AU ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/doc/TMR1995> ;
    tmk:authorityKind "law" ;
    tmk:authorityStatus tmk:Current ;
