<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part32A/2/1/section-53-infringement-of-pbr> a tmk:Chunk,
        tmk:ManualPassage ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/doc/TMM> ;
    tmk:authorityKind "practice" ;
    tmk:capturedIn tmk:snapshot-c490a9927f1a ;
    tmk:chunkKind "body" ;
    tmk:citesProvision <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s16>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s17>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s18>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s19>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s23>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s42(b)>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s46(1)(b)>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s53(1)(c)> ;
    tmk:contentHash "sha256:ad18a0f824c229b2b6ed2cb7e83e80fd4369eb57e5345cd8394e6824dab9bd6d" ;
    tmk:hasCitation <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/cite/TMM/Part32A/2/1/section-53-infringement-of-pbr/prov/0>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/cite/TMM/Part32A/2/1/section-53-infringement-of-pbr/prov/1>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/cite/TMM/Part32A/2/1/section-53-infringement-of-pbr/prov/2>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/cite/TMM/Part32A/2/1/section-53-infringement-of-pbr/prov/3>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/cite/TMM/Part32A/2/1/section-53-infringement-of-pbr/prov/4>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/cite/TMM/Part32A/2/1/section-53-infringement-of-pbr/prov/5>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/cite/TMM/Part32A/2/1/section-53-infringement-of-pbr/prov/6>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/cite/TMM/Part32A/2/1/section-53-infringement-of-pbr/prov/7> ;
    tmk:headingPath "32A.2.1 Section 42: Contrary to Law",
        "Part 32A Examination of Trade Marks for Plants (in Class 31)",
        "Section 53: Infringement of PBR" ;
    tmk:onPage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part32A/2/1> ;
    tmk:ordinal 2 ;
    tmk:partId "Part32A" ;
    tmk:text "(1) Subject to ss 16, 17, 18, 19 and 23, PBR in a plant variety is infringed by: (c) a person using a name of the variety that is entered in the Register in relation to: (i) any other plant variety of the same plant class; or (ii) a plant of any other variety of the same plant class. 1A To avoid doubt, an infringement of PBR in a plant variety under paragraph (1)(c) can include using a synonym in relation to the name of a plant variety, if that synonym is entered in the Register under paragraph 46(1)(b). A ground for rejection under s 42(b) is applicable in the following circumstances: (a) Use of the trade mark would be contrary to s 53(1)(c) of the PBR Act in relation to a plant variety name or synonym of an accepted or granted PBR AND (b) the claimed Class 31 goods are notionally of the plant type for which the PBR is listed AND (c) the owner of the trademark application is a different entity to the title holder of the PBR." ;
    tmk:upstreamRef "TMM/Part32A/2/1/section-53-infringement-of-pbr" .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part34/5/5/1> a tmk:Chunk,
        tmk:ManualPassage ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/doc/TMM> ;
    tmk:authorityKind "practice" ;
    tmk:capturedIn tmk:snapshot-c490a9927f1a ;
    tmk:chunkKind "body" ;
    tmk:citesPassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part30/1>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part31/1>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part32A/1>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part32B/1> ;
    tmk:citesProvision <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s39>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s40>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s42>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s42(b)> ;
    tmk:contentHash "sha256:c56cd525416dc0f54e9cac6988191a577e05c6c34ac37c3044b2ff83bfb067bd" ;
    tmk:hasCitation <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/cite/TMM/Part34/5/5/1/internal/0>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/cite/TMM/Part34/5/5/1/internal/1>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/cite/TMM/Part34/5/5/1/internal/2>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/cite/TMM/Part34/5/5/1/internal/3>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/cite/TMM/Part34/5/5/1/prov/0>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/cite/TMM/Part34/5/5/1/prov/1>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/cite/TMM/Part34/5/5/1/prov/2>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/cite/TMM/Part34/5/5/1/prov/3> ;
    tmk:headingPath "34.5. Grounds for rejection under Division 2 of Part 4 of the Act",
        "5.1 Sections 39, 40 and 42",
        "Part 34 Defensive Trade Marks" ;
    tmk:onPage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part34/5> ;
    tmk:ordinal 2 ;
    tmk:partId "Part34" ;
    tmk:text "Sections 39, 40 and 42 need to be considered in the examination of applications for defensive trade marks. However, as the trade mark must already have been registered otherwise than as a defensive trade mark, it is unlikely that grounds for rejection under these sections will need to be raised. Note: Caution will need to be exercised if the defensive application is in respect of goods to which other legislation is applicable, such as the Plant Breeder’s Rights Act 1994 or the Wine Australia Act 2013. In that case there may be a ground for rejection under paragraph 42(b) which did not apply to the registration upon which the defensive application is based. Part 30 Signs that are Scandalous and Use Contrary to Law Part 31 Prescribed and Prohibited Signs Part 32A Examination of Trade Marks for Plants (in class 31) Part 32B Examination of Trade Marks for Wines (in class 33)" ;
    tmk:upstreamRef "TMM/Part34/5/5/1" .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part46/2%231> a tmk:Chunk,
        tmk:ManualPassage ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/doc/TMM> ;
    tmk:authorityKind "practice" ;
    tmk:capturedIn tmk:snapshot-c490a9927f1a ;
    tmk:chunkKind "body" ;
    tmk:citesPassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part51/x-relevant-legislation3>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part52/x-relevant-legislation2> ;
    tmk:citesProvision <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s54>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s55>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s56>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMR1995/r17A.34M>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMR1995/r17A.34N>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMR1995/r17A.34P> ;
    tmk:contentHash "sha256:4c9f1a0430bfd0a90837b21613eda94966a64b439c426fd31817908cb0589f96" ;
    tmk:hasCitation <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/cite/TMM/Part46/2%231/internal/0>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/cite/TMM/Part46/2%231/internal/1>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/cite/TMM/Part46/2%231/prov/0>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/cite/TMM/Part46/2%231/prov/1>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/cite/TMM/Part46/2%231/prov/2>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/cite/TMM/Part46/2%231/prov/3>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/cite/TMM/Part46/2%231/prov/4>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/cite/TMM/Part46/2%231/prov/5> ;
    tmk:headingPath "Part 46 Grounds for Opposition to Registration or Protection",
        "Part 46.2. The Registrar's role in an opposition" ;
    tmk:onPage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part46/2> ;
    tmk:ordinal 1 ;
    tmk:partId "Part46" ;
    tmk:text "Trade Marks Act 1995 Trade Mark Regulations 1995 Once the opposition commences the parties have set periods in which to file their evidence. Part 51 General Opposition Proceedings When all the evidence periods have ended the parties are given an opportunity to be heard, in person or in writing, by a delegate of the Registrar on the merits of the opposition (section 54 and reg 17A.34M). Following the hearing the delegate, as an administrative decision maker, will decide, on the basis of the evidence and the parties’ submissions, whether or not the opposed trade mark may be registered or protected (section 55 and reg 17A.34N). Part 52 Hearings, Decisions, Reasons and Appeals The delegate’s decision may be appealed in the Federal Court or the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 2) (section 56 and reg 17A.34P)." ;
    tmk:upstreamRef "TMM/Part46/2#1" .

