        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/cite/TMM/Part17/2/2/1/prov/7>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/cite/TMM/Part17/2/2/1/prov/8>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/cite/TMM/Part17/2/2/1/prov/9> ;
    tmk:headingPath "17.2. Circumstances under which deferments will be granted",
        "2.1 Grounds upon which an applicant may apply for deferment",
        "Part 17 Deferment of Acceptance" ;
    tmk:onPage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part17/2> ;
    tmk:ordinal 2 ;
    tmk:partId "Part17" ;
    tmk:text "2.1.1 Where a citation has been raised against an application under subsection 44(1) or (2) on the basis of a prior application/s and the applicant is awaiting finalisation of the cited application/s (subreg 4.13(1)(c)(i)). The Registrar will exercise their discretion not to grant deferment under this provision where two applications are cited against each other that have the same filing date. • Part 26 Conflict with other Signs - Section 44 - 7. Trade marks with the same priority date 2.1.2 Where a citation has been raised against an application under subsection 44(1) or (2) and the applicant is seeking to establish “honest concurrent use”, “prior use” or “other circumstances” of their own trade mark under subsections 44(3) or 44(4) respectively (subreg 4.13(1)(c)(ii)). • Where multiple citations have been raised, it is expected that evidence of use or other circumstances be gathered concurrently for all citations. That is, an application for deferment under subregulation 4.13(1)(c)(ii) applies to all citations collectively and is not applied separately to each citation. • If deferment of acceptance has been previously granted under subregulation 4.13(1)(c)(ii), then changing to another approach still covered by this provision, such as shifting from gathering evidence of “prior use” to “other circumstances”, is not regarded as a new reason for a new deferment application. 2.1.3 Where a citation has been raised against an application under subsection 44(1) or (2) and the applicant has filed, under section 92 of the Act, a non-use application in respect of a trade mark that has been cited against the applicant's trade mark and the applicant is awaiting the finalisation of the non-use application (subreg 4.13(1)(c)(iii)). 2.1.4 Where a citation has been raised against an application under subsection 44(1) or (2) and an action by the applicant for rectification of the Register regarding the cited trade mark is pending (subreg 4.13(1)(c)(iv)). 2.1.5 Where a citation has been raised against an application under subsection 44(1) or (2) and the cited trade mark is un-renewed but is within 6 months of its expiry date under the terms of section 79 of the Act (subreg 4.13(1)(c)(v))." ;
    tmk:upstreamRef "TMM/Part17/2/2/1" .

