    tmk:headingPath "15.1. When the general provision applies",
        "Part 15 General Provision for Extensions of Time" ;
    tmk:onPage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part15/1> ;
    tmk:ordinal 2 ;
    tmk:partId "Part15" ;
    tmk:text "filing a notice of opposition to an amendment of a trade mark application which has been published for opposition (section 65A and reg 6.6). Part 9 Amendments and Changes of Address - 4. Amendment after particulars of an application have been published (Sections 63, 65 and 65A) filing an application for an award of costs, or a bill of costs in relation to opposition proceedings (reg 21.12) requesting an extension to a cooling-off period (reg 5.16) registration of a trade mark (reg 7.1) Part 39 Registration of a Trade Mark - 4. Timing for Registration claiming a right or interest in a trade mark to respond to a notification regarding cancellation of registration of the trade mark (section 84 and subregs 8.1(2) and (3)), assignment or transmission of the trade mark (section 111 and reg 10.5), or a request to cancel the recordal of the claimed interest (section 115 and subreg 11.3(4)). filing a notice of opposition to an amendment of a trade mark registration which has been published for opposition (section 83A and reg 8.4)." ;
    tmk:upstreamRef "TMM/Part15/1#1~2" .

