        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/cite/TMM/Part30/x-annex-a1---examples-of-legislation-which-may-trigger-the-provisions-of-section-42b%231/prov/9> ;
    tmk:headingPath "30. Annex A1 - Examples of Legislation which may trigger the provisions of section 42(b)",
        "Part 30 Signs that are Scandalous and Use Contrary to Law" ;
    tmk:onPage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part30/x-annex-a1---examples-of-legislation-which-may-trigger-the-provisions-of-section-42b> ;
    tmk:ordinal 1 ;
    tmk:partId "Part30" ;
    tmk:text "Advance Australia Logo Protection Act 1984 (Cth) section 11 Agricultural and Veterinary Chemicals Code Act 1994 (Cth) section 170A Australian and Overseas Telecommunications Corporation Act 1991 (Cth) section 15 Banking Act 1959 (Cth), sections 66 and 66A Commonwealth Games Arrangements Act 2011 (Queensland) section 51 Competition and Consumer Act 2010 (Cth) (formerly the Trade Practices Act 1974 (Cth)) Copyright Act 1968 (Cth) Country of Origin Food Labelling Information Standard 2016 (Cth) Crimes (Currency) Act 1981 (Cth) Defence Act 1903 (Cth) section 83 Defence Regulations 2016 (Cth) part 14 Environment Protection and Biodiversity Conservation Act 1999 (Cth) and Regulation 12.38 of Environment Protection and Biodiversity Conservation Regulations 2000 (Cth) Flags Act 1953 (Cth) section 6 Food Standards Australia New Zealand Act 1991 (Cth) (Australian New Zealand Food Standards Code – Standard 1.4.4) Geneva Conventions Act 1957 (Cth) section 15 Health Insurance Commission Act 1973 (Cth) section 41(c) Human Services (Centrelink) Act 1997 (Cth) section 38 International Organizations (Privileges and Immunities) Act 1963 (Cth) section 12 Life Insurance Act 1995 (Cth) section 16E Major Sporting Events (Indicia and Images) Protection Act 2014 (Cth) National Occupational Health and Safety Commission Act 1985 (Cth) National Occupational Health and Safety Commission Regulations 1986 (Cth) sections 7 and 8 Olympic Insignia Protection Act 1987 (Cth) section 19 Plant Breeder's Rights Act 1994 (Cth) section 53 Scout Association Act 1924 (Cth) sections 2 and 4 Telecommunications Act 1997 (Cth) section 417 Telstra Corporation Act 1991 (Cth) section 15 Protection of Word ‘Anzac’ Act 1920 (Cth) and Protection of Word 'ANZAC' Regulations (Cth), regulation 2 Wine Australia Act 2013 (Cth) (formerly the Australian Grape and Wine Authority Act 2013 (Cth) and Wine Australia Corporation Act 1980 (Cth))" ;
    tmk:upstreamRef "TMM/Part30/x-annex-a1---examples-of-legislation-which-may-trigger-the-provisions-of-section-42b#1" .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMR1995/r4.15> a tmk:LegislativeProvision ;
    rdfs:label "Trade marks containing etc certain signs"@en-AU ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/doc/TMR1995> ;
    tmk:authorityKind "law" ;
    tmk:authorityStatus tmk:Current ;
    tmk:capturedIn tmk:snapshot-c490a9927f1a ;
    tmk:contentHash "sha256:0e92a39730130410d615b5f180f4a106dc23cdb64f50e608b9d8253101fc1c50" ;
    tmk:text "For the purposes of paragraph 39(2)(a) of the Act (which deals with signs), the following signs are prescribed: (a) the words ‘Patent’, ‘Patented’, ‘By Royal Letters Patent’, ‘Protected International Trade Mark’, ‘Registered’, ‘Registered Design’, ‘Copyright’ ‘Plant Breeder’s Rights’, ‘EL rights’, or words or symbols to the same effect (including the symbols ‘©’ and ‘®’); (b) the words ‘To counterfeit this is a forgery’, or words to the same effect; (c) a representation of the Arms, or of a flag or seal, of the Commonwealth or of a State or Territory; (d) a representation of the Arms or emblem of a city or town in Australia or of a public authority or public institution in Australia; (da) a representation of a flag of a country that is a member of the International Union for the Protection of Industrial Property; (e) a representation of a mark notified by the International Union for the Protection of Industrial Property as not entitled to registration under international arrangements; (f) a sign specified in Schedule 2. Note 1: For the meaning of EL rights, see section 5 of the Circuit Layouts Act 1989. Note 2: A list of the marks mentioned in paragraph 4.15(e) is available at the Trade Marks Office and suboffices (if any)." ;
    tmk:upstreamRef "TMR1995/r4.15" .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMR1995/r9.2> a tmk:LegislativeProvision ;
    rdfs:label "Definitions"@en-AU ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/doc/TMR1995> ;
    tmk:authorityKind "law" ;
    tmk:authorityStatus tmk:Current ;
    tmk:capturedIn tmk:snapshot-c490a9927f1a ;
    tmk:contentHash "sha256:01a55dee69f90ac66ec163cf44c704e348b6c3fec5279ecefaea3e2225e24ebd" ;
    tmk:text "In this Part: application for removal means an application for removal of a trade mark from the Register. notice of intention to defend means a notice filed under regulation 9.15. notice of opposition means a notice of opposition under section 96 of the Act. opponent means a person who files: (a) a notice of intention to oppose; and (b) a statement of grounds and particulars. party means an applicant or opponent. statement of grounds and particulars means a statement by an opponent that sets out: (a) the grounds for removal that the opponent intends to rebut; and (b) the facts and circumstances that form the basis for the opposition to the removal. Note: The following terms are defined in section 6 of the Act: (a) applicant; (b) approved form; (c) employee; (d) file; (e) month; (f) person." ;
    tmk:upstreamRef "TMR1995/r9.2" .

